{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The problem contains a sure outcome (Lottery A: 500 Euros with 100% probability), so the reference value is 500 Euros. For Lottery A, the only outcome is equal to the reference value, so the difference is 0 with 100% probability. For Lottery B, the outcomes are 1000 Euros (difference of +500 with 50% probability) and 0 Euros (difference of -500 with 50% probability). The mean difference for Lottery B is (0.5 × +500) + (0.5 × -500) = 0. The mean difference for Lottery A is 0. Thus, both lotteries have the same mean difference (0), so the decision reason would be indifferent between A and B.",
